        <div class="callout">
          <p class="eyebrow">The first step</p>
          <h2>The security check: where do you really stand?</h2>
          <p class="callout-sub">A complete small first step, not an open-ended consulting appointment.</p>
          <p class="lead">I come to you and look at what you have, that is servers, network, access and backups, and check whether it holds up to what you assume. Without interfering with your running operations.</p>
          <p>What you know afterwards:</p>
          <ul class="why-points">
            <li><strong>Whether your backups hold in an emergency.</strong> I actually restore one of them, on your behalf, in an isolated environment. Verified, not claimed.</li>
            <li><strong>Which systems aren't backed up at all.</strong> That's more common than people think.</li>
            <li><strong>Where access is open</strong> that shouldn't be.</li>
            <li><strong>What should come first,</strong> what can wait, and roughly what it costs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="callout-note">The scope is small and clearly defined. You get a fixed offer in advance, no open-ended invoice and no follow-up obligation. The written report is yours; you can also present it to another provider.</p>
